/-!
# Exact weak closure of the native common-time replay

The source-owned whole residual already generates a finite terminal replay
or an infinite strictly refining support lineage.  This module connects the
infinite branch to the existing whole-carrier compactness and weak Fourier
consumer without replacing its physical trajectories:

* every replay stage is recompiled as a half-critical generated path;
* common-time finite Galerkin uniqueness identifies the canonical compactness
  trajectory with the original actual replay trajectory;
* one whole-carrier subsequence therefore converges for the original replay;
* every Fourier row actually generated by the support lineage eventually
  remains present and satisfies the all-tests weak identity.

No target state, subsequence, trajectory, coverage certificate, cutoff,
critical margin, or branch is supplied by a caller.
-/

